ARTIFACT (native parity port of features/dashboard/widgets/DriveScoreGaugeWidget.tsx)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
New files (compiled into the iOS + macOS app targets via project.yml `Sources` glob):
  apps/apple/Sources/DashboardWidgets/DriveScoreGaugeWidget.swift       (container + pure DriveScoreGaugeContent presentation, all states)
  apps/apple/Sources/DashboardWidgets/DriveScoreGaugeWidgetViews.swift  (gauge hero, radial gauge, sub-score bars, 7 #Previews)
  apps/apple/Sources/DashboardWidgets/DriveScoreGaugeWidgetModel.swift  (state-holder-bound @Observable model + P1/S11 telemetry seam + ViewOpenRecorder)
  apps/apple/Sources/DashboardWidgets/DriveScoreGaugeWidgetData.swift   (DriveScoreProjection adapter, score tone, render-state derivation, registry/size)
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/DashboardWidgets/DriveScoreGaugeWidgetTests.swift (29 tests: adapter + per-state + registry + telemetry + a11y)

Parity notes:
- Data sources: binds shared P1/S8 `DrivingStore.driveScore(vehicleId:)` (web `useDriveScore`)
  through `StateHolderModel` + `LoadableState` (mirrors the representative VehicleSettingsModel).
  No direct HTTP from the view. `useVehicles`/vehicle selection handled by the injected vehicleID.
- Shared components mapped: @/components/data-display -> TSMetricBar/TSMetricLabel; @/components/feedback
  -> TSEmptyState/TSQueryError/TSSkeleton/TSFreshnessIndicator. Web RadialGauge/WidgetGaugeHero ->
  native DriveScoreGauge + DriveScoreGaugeHero (SwiftUI Shape arc; no third-party chart needed; prompt lists charts=none).
- States reproduced: loading (skeleton chrome), loaded, empty ("No score yet"), error (QueryError + retry),
  stale (Stale chip), offline (cached value + Offline chip). Compact (1x1) and tall (>=2 rows) variants.
- i18n: every source string resolves through the P1/S10 catalog (apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings,
  generated from apps/shared/i18n/catalog). Keys: translation.widget.driveScoreGauge.{title,weekly,efficiency,
  smoothness,speed,noData} (+ chrome: widget.freshness.stale/offline, translation.common.refresh). A unit test
  asserts each key resolves (does NOT fall back to the raw key). No English literals in native code.
- a11y: VoiceOver labels/values on the gauge, refresh control, freshness chips; Dynamic Type via tokens;
  reduce-motion respected on the gauge animation.
- Telemetry (P1/S11): emits view.opened as the typed TelemetryEvent.ScreenView(screen:"DriveScoreGaugeWidget")
  via the shared consent-gated Telemetry, exactly once per appearance (ViewOpenRecorder; spy-tested).
- Registry: DriveScoreGaugeRegistry mirrors registry/driving.ts `drive-score-gauge` — default 1x2, min 1x2,
  max 2x40, category driving; clamp() enforces the min..max box (tested).
Change surface is purely ADDITIVE (git status: only the two new dirs; zero existing files modified) ->
existing behavior cannot regress.

